+## Optional session hydration
+
+Before the first live baseline, an embedding may provide the optional `sessionHydration` adapter. Its synchronous list/window seeds are display-only and never authoritative; adapter exceptions are swallowed at this seam so normal live Session operation remains available. Successful live list, history, stream, and paging changes are committed back through the adapter without assigning persistence policy to the runtime.
+
+`sessionBaselineReadiness` is a replayable snapshot store keyed by connection generation. A generation is `ready` only after its own live list baseline and the currently selected history baseline succeed; a failed later refresh publishes `error` even if an older generation had been ready. Cached rows and pending interactions do not satisfy readiness.
+
